## STEP 60 — False Positive Corpus

Build a deliberately safe application containing behaviors that commonly fool scanners:

* custom 404 returning 200
* generic JSON success envelope
* SPA fallback
* reflected text that is HTML-encoded
* public IDs
* shared resources
* permissive CORS on public non-sensitive endpoint
* CSP nonce setup
* rate limiting with unusual status codes
* generic DB-looking error text
* fake secrets in documentation
* source maps with no secret material

Magic_Security must not incorrectly report verified vulnerabilities.

