## STEP 62 — Backtesting Acceptance Sequence

Create one automated test that performs the complete security history lifecycle:

1. Scan clean version.
2. Set baseline.
3. Introduce vulnerability.
4. Scan.
5. Assert `NEW`.
6. Fix vulnerability.
7. Scan.
8. Assert `RESOLVED`.
9. Reintroduce vulnerability.
10. Scan.
11. Assert `REINTRODUCED`.
12. Increase severity.
13. Assert `WORSENED`.
14. Disable browser/auth coverage.
15. Assert scan is not coverage-equivalent.

This should be a real end-to-end test, not only handcrafted snapshot dictionaries.

